sections.s5b_flow:
```
  ═══ WHY DEFAULT METHODS WERE ADDED (backward compatibility) ═══

  BEFORE Java 8:
    interface Iterable<T> {
        Iterator<T> iterator();             // the ONLY method
    }
    // ArrayList, LinkedList, HashSet, TreeSet... 50+ classes implement this

  PROBLEM: Java 8 wants to add forEach():
    interface Iterable<T> {
        Iterator<T> iterator();
        void forEach(Consumer<T> action);   // NEW abstract → 50+ classes BREAK!
    }

  SOLUTION: default method!
    interface Iterable<T> {
        Iterator<T> iterator();
        default void forEach(Consumer<T> action) {  // has body → no break!
            for (T t : this) { action.accept(t); }
        }
    }
    // Result: ArrayList.forEach(), HashSet.forEach() → work immediately, zero code change.

  ═══ OUR BANKING EXAMPLE ═══

  interface AccountService {
      Account getAccount(String id);              // ABSTRACT — day 1

      default String getFormattedBalance(id);     // DEFAULT — added later, FREE
      default String getBalanceAlert(id);          // DEFAULT — added later, FREE
      default AccountSummary getSummary(id);       // DEFAULT — composes other defaults

      static BigDecimal calculateInterest(...);    // STATIC — utility, NOT inherited
  }

  SavingsAccountService implements AccountService:
    ├─ getAccount() → OVERRIDES (loads from DB)
    ├─ getFormattedBalance() → INHERITED default (₹1,25,000.50)
    ├─ getBalanceAlert() → INHERITED default
    └─ getSummary() → INHERITED default

  CurrentAccountService implements AccountService:
    ├─ getAccount() → OVERRIDES (loads from DB)
    ├─ getFormattedBalance() → OVERRIDES ("Business Balance: ₹...")
    ├─ getBalanceAlert() → INHERITED default
    └─ getSummary() → INHERITED default → but calls OVERRIDDEN getFormattedBalance()!

  ═══ DEFAULT vs STATIC ═══

  DEFAULT:                              STATIC:
  ├─ Has body (Recommended) ├─ Has body (Recommended) 
  ├─ Inherited by impls (Recommended) ├─ NOT inherited (Avoid) 
  ├─ Can be overridden (Recommended) ├─ Cannot be overridden (Avoid) 
  ├─ Called via instance (Recommended) ├─ Called via InterfaceName.method() (Recommended) 
  └─ Can access `this` (Recommended) └─ Cannot access `this` (Avoid) 
```
